# CLAUDE.md

Per-repo orientation for `${git_provider.org}/${project_name}`. Cross-cutting
context lives in [homelab/docs](https://${git_provider.host}/${git_provider.org}/docs);
this file documents what's universal to every homelab repo plus what's
specific to this one. Type-specific content is appended below the
"Repo-specific" marker.

## Homelab universals (apply to every homelab repo)

### Toolchain

- **Pinned via `mise.toml`**. Run `mise install` before anything.
- **Task runner: `just`**. `just` (no args) shows the menu. Recipes use
  positional dispatch (`just packer talos beelink`, not
  `just packer-talos-beelink`).

### Secrets

- **`.env` is a [1Password Developer Environment](https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/local-env-file) file**.
  `OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN` is a literal value; everything else is an
  `op://` reference resolved at command time by
  `op run --env-file=.env -- <cmd>`. See `.env.example`.
- **Never `source .env`** — it loads the literal `op://...` strings,
  which is not what tools want.
- **`OnePasswordItem` CRs** point to 1Password items via
  `vaults/<id>/items/<id>`. Get IDs via
  `op item get <name> --format json`.

### Documentation

- **`docz create <type> "Title"`** for ADR / RFC / DESIGN / IMPL / INV.
  Handles frontmatter, README index, mkdocs nav.
- **Repo-local docs live in `docs/`**; cross-cutting topics (runbooks,
  network topology, storage guides) live in
  [homelab/docs](https://${git_provider.host}/${git_provider.org}/docs).
- **Backstage TechDocs**: `catalog-info.yaml` registers this repo as a
  Component with `backstage.io/techdocs-ref: dir:.`. mkdocs builds the
  site; Backstage renders it.

### Conventions (apply across all homelab repos)

- **Small, reversible commits** beat bundled PRs. Roll back by reverting.
- **For Argo-synced manifests**: commit straight to `main` (trunk-based).
  PR review delays sync — for live cluster state, that's worse than a
  direct push. Other manifest types follow normal PR flow.
- **Capture cross-cutting surprises in the active IMPL's Follow-Ups
  section** — don't silently work around a bug and move on.
- **Plans first for non-trivial work** — write an IMPL or DESIGN doc,
  get review, then implement.
- **`labels.yaml` + `gitea-label-sync`** keeps issue/PR labels
  canonical across the homelab fleet. Forgejo repos use
  `--platform=forgejo`; `homelab-tools` uses `--platform=github`.
- **Renovate** manages dep updates. Custom regex managers fire on
  `mise.toml`, `docker-bake.hcl`, helm `Chart.yaml`, `.typ` — annotate
  pinned versions with `# renovate: image=<repo>` (or equivalent) one
  line above the version literal.
- **Linters**: `yamllint` + `markdownlint-cli2` + `prettier` + (where
  relevant) `tflint` / `checkmake`. Run via `just lint`.

### Operating notes (universal gotchas)

- **`grep` is `rg`**. The user aliases `grep` → `ripgrep`; regex is the
  default. Drop `-E` from commands.
- **Verify CRD schema, don't grep rendered YAML**. Use
  `kubectl explain <crd>.spec --recursive` or
  `kubectl get crd <name> -o jsonpath='{...}'` against the live CRD.
  Reading chart example YAML is brittle and frequently wrong for
  alpha APIs.
- **Alpha-API debug loop discipline**: when one schema error reveals
  the next, stop and dump the full schema. Don't iterate one field at
  a time.
- **RWO PVC + single-replica Deployment**: default `strategy: Recreate`,
  not RollingUpdate. RollingUpdate deadlocks because the new pod can't
  attach the volume while the old one still holds it.

### Homelab repo map

- `${git_provider.org}/k8s` — ArgoCD-managed kustomize manifests
- `${git_provider.org}/tf-modules` — Terraform modules, SemVer-tagged
- `${git_provider.org}/tf-live` — Terragrunt live + Atlantis plan/apply
- `${git_provider.org}/images` — Packer image builds
- `${git_provider.org}/charts` — Helm charts (OCI to Harbor + Forgejo Packages)
- `${git_provider.org}/infra` — Non-IaC config (Talos, network, Proxmox, servers)
- `${git_provider.org}/docs` — Docusaurus aggregator (cross-cutting docs)
- `${git_provider.org}/tools` — Go CLIs (forgejo primary, GitHub mirror planned)

